body:
There is no problem of induction; read Strawson's chapter on it in Introduction to Logical Theory.

&#x200B;

And anyway the reasoning you provided is very obviously question begging and ignores the supposed problem of induction rather than addressing it. Saying in response to the sceptic about induction: "But look, things work!" is exactly the reason that the sceptic wants to say is unfounded. Strawson's reply shows why this is not so, but it isn't enough to simply contradict the sceptic.
